A||||3||CRAGAR||Scan computer for ALDL connector?||||1
Z||000000||CRAGAR||09-20-1999||12:59 PM||||I'm looking for a "Scan tool" (computer) that connects into the ALDL connector in the center console.  Can you recommend a place to purchase one? part number? description? and price"?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-20-1999||01:55 PM||||code retrievers, a waste of money for fiero, are available at any parts store or Wall mart. Code retrievers do just that, and only that. These are 20-30$us<P>The only reasonably priced scanner I've found is AutoXray GM scanner. This unit only works on GM cars. It comes complete with cable for 150-180$us. Strauss discount auto has them. Easwood, <A HREF="http://www.eastwoodco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.eastwoodco.com</A>  also has them. Thesed units can read the state any sensor or control line the ECM has. It can monitor in real time but some ECM's can't handle realtime data and driving at the same time.<P>AutoXray also has a universal scanner that starts at about 250$us Plus 30$ for each cable you need. Other universal scanners, like Actron's, are similar||||reg||1
Z||000002||CRAGAR||09-21-1999||02:37 PM||||theogre, can the AutoXray scanner be used to set the timing?  I know that timing (advance) is one of the outputs of these scan computers.  Do you think its real time enough to actually set the timing?  It seems like it would be alot less hassle than a timing light and more accurate.  Thanks for your response.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-21-1999||02:58 PM||||Fiero ECM's are not setable for anything via the ALDL connector. The ALDL can only be used to monitor the ECM.||||reg||1
